Chapter: Sass89Int
  cites Sass chapter SassCtrl
  cites Sass chapter Sass89Hmma

 SM 8.9 integer, move, memory and exit encodings for a first kernel, from
 Mesa 26.2.4 nak/sm70_encode.rs (encode_alu_base, OpMov, OpIAdd3, OpIAdd3X,
 OpISetP, OpShf, OpS2R, OpLdc, OpLd, OpSt, OpExit, set_mem_order). Bits are
 numbered over the 128-bit instruction: the first word holds 0..63, the
 second 64..127, each little-endian; controls occupy 105..125 as in
 Sass89Hmma.

 ALU fields: opcode 0..8 and source form 9..11 (register 1, 32-bit immediate
 4, constant bank 5); guard predicate 12..14, negated at 15; destination
 16..23; source 0 at 24..31, negated at 72; source 1 at 32..39 (negated at
 63), or an immediate in 32..63, or c[bank][offset] with the byte offset at
 38..53 and the bank at 54..58; source 2 at 64..71. Register 255 is RZ.

 IADD3 (opcode 0x10): .X at 74; carry-in predicates at 87..89 (not 90) and
 77..79 (not 80), PT negated when absent; carry-out predicates at 81..83 and
 84..86, PT when absent. ISETP (0x0C): low-compare predicate 68..70 (not 71),
 PT here since .EX is not admitted; signed at 73; AND 0, OR 1, XOR 2 at
 74..75; LT 1, EQ 2, LE 3, GT 4, NE 5, GE 6 at 76..78; the accumulated
 predicate at 87..89 (not 90); the result at 81..83, PT at 84..86. SHF
 (0x19): type at 73..74 (S64 0, S32 2, U32 3), right at 76, .HI at 80, wrap
 at 75 left clear. U64 is refused: NAK writes 1, turingas 0 for the same
 spelling. MOV (0x02) writes all four quad lanes, 0xF at 72..75. IMAD
 (0x24) and IMAD.WIDE (0x25, a register-pair destination and addend):
 signed at 73, PT at 81..83, and !PT at 87..90, which turingas writes and
 NAK leaves clear.

 PRMT (0x16): the selector as source 1, the second word as source 2, index
 mode (0 at 72..74). LOP3 (0x12): the truth table at 72..79, PT at 81..83,
 !PT at 87..90, which turingas writes only when the predicate is spelled.

 Shared memory takes a 32-bit address register and the 24-bit signed byte
 offset at 40..63, with the type at 73..75. LDS is 0x984 with uniform
 addressing (91) clear, the only LDS form turingas encodes; NAK at SM 8.9
 sets 91 with URZ at 32..37, and whether Ada reads the clear form is a
 hardware question. STS is NAK's SM 8.9 form, 0x988: data 32..39, URZ at
 64..69, uniform addressing at 91. BAR.SYNC (0xB1D) is barrier 0, every
 other field clear, in both.

 BRA (0x947): the byte offset from the next instruction, a multiple of 16,
 sign-extended over 32..81 (NAK writes it as words at 34..81, and .U at 32
 clear); the branch condition PT at 87..89, the guard deciding.

 FADD (0x21) and FMUL (0x20) are the ALU layout with register sources,
 source 1 negated at 63; rounding (78..79) to nearest, no saturation (77)
 and no flush to zero (80) leave the second word clear. FMNMX (0x09)
 takes max with !PT at 87..90 (PT is min). MUFU (0x108) and F2F (0x104)
 read their source as source 1; MUFU's function is at 74..77 (EX2 2, LG2
 3), and F2F.F16.F32's second word is turingas's 0x200800.

 LDGSTS (0xFAE), the asynchronous global-to-shared copy, is turingas's
 form: the shared address register at 16..23, the global address pair at
 24..31, and turingas's fixed second word 0x0F901C48 (the 128-bit type at
 73..75 and its constant bits, which it writes the same for .E and
 .BYPASS, and !PT at 87..90). Which cache path and what that predicate
 select on Ada is a hardware question. LDGDEPBAR (0x9AF) has no field;
 DEPBAR (0x91A) .LE at 47, scoreboard SB0, and its count at 38..43.

 WARPSYNC is NAK's (OpWarpSync, encode_alu_base): opcode 0x148 in form 4,
 the 32-bit mask at 32..63, no destination or source 0, and the predicate
 PT at 87..89 (not at 90). turingas has no WARPSYNC, so the listing tags
 the line N and the grade checks these fields instead.

 S2R (0x919): the system register at 72..79. LDC (0xB82): offset register RZ
 at 24..31, the constant at 38..58, the memory type at 73..75 (32 bits 4, 64
 bits 5). EXIT (0x94D): PT at 87..89.

 LDG is NAK's SM 8.9 form, 0x981: address register 24..31, 64-bit address
 at 90, uniform offset register URZ (63) at 32..37 taken as 64-bit at 72,
 the byte offset (24 bits, signed) at 40..63, the result predicate PT at
 81..83, uniform addressing at 91. STG is 0x386, the form turingas encodes
 from NVIDIA's own SM 7.5 output and NAK writes below SM 7.3: address
 24..31, 64-bit address at 72, data 32..39, the byte offset at 40..63.
 Whether Ada executes 0x386 is a hardware question. Both carry the memory
 type at 73..75 (16 bits zero-extended 2, 32 bits 4, 64 bits 5), the memory order at 77..80 and the eviction priority at
 84..86, written normal (1): turingas at f7c1a74 looks up .EF and .LU without
 their dot and encodes no other priority. The order is NAK's SM 8.0+ table:
 weak 0, constant 4, strong GPU 7, strong system 10; strong CTA (5) is
 refused because turingas's scope field cannot spell it.

Section: Instructions

  S89Src =
   | S89Reg (Integer)
   | S89Imm (Integer)
   | S89Cb (Integer) (Integer)

  S89Add = record {
   dst : Integer,
   a : Integer,
   a-neg : Integer,
   b : S89Src,
   b-neg : Integer,
   c : Integer,
   x : Integer,
   out0 : Integer,
   out1 : Integer,
   in0 : Integer,
   in0-neg : Integer,
   in1 : Integer,
   in1-neg : Integer
  }

  S89Cmp = record {
   pred : Integer,
   cmp : Integer,
   signed : Integer,
   bool-op : Integer,
   a : Integer,
   b : S89Src,
   accum : Integer,
   accum-neg : Integer
  }

  S89Shift = record {
   dst : Integer,
   right : Integer,
   kind : Integer,
   high-half : Integer,
   low : Integer,
   shift : S89Src,
   high : Integer
  }

  S89Mad = record {
   dst : Integer,
   a : Integer,
   b : S89Src,
   c : Integer,
   wide : Integer,
   signed : Integer
  }

  S89Mem = record {
   data : Integer,
   addr : Integer,
   offset : Integer,
   width : Integer,
   order : Integer
  }

  S89Body =
   | S89Mov (Integer) (S89Src)
   | S89Iadd3 (S89Add)
   | S89Imad (S89Mad)
   | S89Prmt (Integer) (Integer) (S89Src) (Integer)
   | S89Lop3 (Integer) (Integer) (S89Src) (Integer) (Integer)
   | S89Isetp (S89Cmp)
   | S89Shf (S89Shift)
   | S89S2r (Integer) (Integer)
   | S89Ldc (Integer) (Integer) (Integer) (Integer)
   | S89Ldg (S89Mem)
   | S89Stg (S89Mem)
   | S89Lds (S89Mem)
   | S89Sts (S89Mem)
   | S89Bar
   | S89Hmma (Integer) (Integer) (Integer) (Integer)
   | S89Fadd (Integer) (Integer) (Integer) (Integer)
   | S89Fmul (Integer) (Integer) (Integer)
   | S89Fmax (Integer) (Integer) (Integer)
   | S89Mufu (Integer) (Integer) (Integer)
   | S89F2fh (Integer) (Integer)
   | S89Ldgsts (Integer) (Integer)
   | S89LdgDepbar
   | S89Depbar (Integer)
   | S89Warpsync (Integer)
   | S89Bra (Integer)
   | S89Exit

  S89Insn = record {
   body : S89Body,
   guard : Integer,
   guard-neg : Integer,
   control : CtrlCode
  }

Section: Validity

  s89-in : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  s89-in (v) (lo) (hi) = if v < lo then False else v <= hi

  s89-reg : Integer -> Boolean
  s89-reg (r) = s89-in r 0 255

  s89-pair : Integer -> Boolean
  s89-pair (r) = if s89-in r 0 253 == False then False else bit-and r 1 == 0

  s89-pred : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  s89-pred (p) (neg) = if s89-in p 0 7 == False then False else s89-in neg 0 1

  s89-src-error : S89Src, Integer -> Text
  s89-src-error (s) (neg) =
    if s89-in neg 0 1 == False then "source"
    else when s
     is S89Reg (r) -> if s89-reg r then "" else "register"
     is S89Imm (v) -> if neg == 1 then "source" else if s89-in v -2147483648 #FFFFFFFF then "" else "source"
     is S89Cb (bank) (off) -> if s89-in bank 0 31 == False then "source" else if s89-in off 0 #FFFC == False then "source" else if bit-and off 3 == 0 then "" else "source"

  s89-src-is-reg : S89Src -> Boolean
  s89-src-is-reg (s) =
    when s
     is S89Reg (r) -> True
     is otherwise -> False

  s89-sys-ok : Integer -> Boolean
  s89-sys-ok (id) = if id == 0 then True else if s89-in id 33 35 then True else s89-in id 37 39

  s89-order-ok : Integer -> Boolean
  s89-order-ok (o) = if o == 0 then True else if o == 4 then True else if o == 7 then True else o == 10

  s89-wide-ok : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  s89-wide-ok (r) (width) =
    if width == 16 | width == 32 then s89-reg r else if width == 64 then s89-pair r else False

  s89-add-error : S89Add -> Text
  s89-add-error (i) =
    let src = s89-src-error i.b i.b-neg
    in if src /= "" then src
    else if s89-reg i.dst == False | s89-reg i.a == False | s89-reg i.c == False then "register"
    else if s89-in i.a-neg 0 1 == False | s89-in i.x 0 1 == False then "modifier"
    else if i.a-neg == 1 & i.b-neg == 1 then "modifier"
    else if s89-pred i.out0 0 == False | s89-pred i.out1 0 == False then "predicate"
    else if s89-pred i.in0 i.in0-neg == False | s89-pred i.in1 i.in1-neg == False then "predicate"
    else if i.x == 0 & (i.in0 /= 7 | i.in0-neg /= 1 | i.in1 /= 7 | i.in1-neg /= 1) then "predicate"
    else ""

  s89-mad-error : S89Mad -> Text
  s89-mad-error (i) =
    let src = s89-src-error i.b 0
    in if src /= "" then src
    else if s89-reg i.a == False | s89-reg i.c == False | s89-reg i.dst == False then "register"
    else if s89-in i.wide 0 1 == False | s89-in i.signed 0 1 == False then "modifier"
    else if i.wide == 1 & (s89-pair i.dst == False | (i.c /= 255 & s89-pair i.c == False)) then "register"
    else ""

  s89-three-error : Integer, Integer, S89Src, Integer, Integer -> Text
  s89-three-error (d) (a) (s) (c) (neg) =
    let src = s89-src-error s neg
    in if src /= "" then src
    else if s89-reg d == False | s89-reg a == False | s89-reg c == False then "register"
    else ""

  s89-cmp-error : S89Cmp -> Text
  s89-cmp-error (i) =
    let src = s89-src-error i.b 0
    in if src /= "" then src
    else if s89-reg i.a == False then "register"
    else if s89-in i.pred 0 7 == False | s89-pred i.accum i.accum-neg == False then "predicate"
    else if s89-in i.cmp 1 6 == False | s89-in i.signed 0 1 == False | s89-in i.bool-op 0 2 == False then "modifier"
    else ""

  s89-amount-error : S89Src -> Text
  s89-amount-error (s) =
    when s
     is S89Imm (v) -> if s89-in v 0 63 then "" else "source"
     is otherwise -> s89-src-error s 0

  s89-shift-error : S89Shift -> Text
  s89-shift-error (i) =
    let src = s89-amount-error i.shift
    in if src /= "" then src
    else if s89-reg i.dst == False | s89-reg i.low == False | s89-reg i.high == False then "register"
    else if s89-in i.right 0 1 == False | s89-in i.high-half 0 1 == False then "modifier"
    else if i.kind == 1 then "type"
    else if i.kind /= 0 & i.kind /= 2 & i.kind /= 3 then "type"
    else ""

  s89-mem-error : S89Mem -> Text
  s89-mem-error (m) =
    if s89-pair m.addr == False then "register"
    else if s89-wide-ok m.data m.width == False then "register"
    else if s89-in m.offset -8388608 8388607 == False then "offset"
    else if s89-order-ok m.order == False then "order"
    else ""

  s89-shared-error : S89Mem -> Text
  s89-shared-error (m) =
    if s89-reg m.addr == False then "register"
    else if s89-wide-ok m.data m.width == False then "register"
    else if s89-in m.offset -8388608 8388607 == False then "offset"
    else if m.order /= 7 then "order"
    else ""

  s89-ldc-error : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  s89-ldc-error (d) (width) (bank) (off) =
    if width == 16 then "width"
    else if s89-wide-ok d width == False then "register"
    else if s89-in bank 0 31 == False | s89-in off 0 #FFFF == False then "source"
    else if int-mod off (width / 8) /= 0 then "source"
    else ""

 The reuse flags a source may carry: bit 0 source 0, bit 1 source 1, bit 2
 source 2, each only on a register.

  s89-reuse-mask : S89Body -> Integer
  s89-reuse-mask (b) =
    when b
     is S89Mov (d) (s) -> if s89-src-is-reg s then 2 else 0
     is S89Iadd3 (i) -> if s89-src-is-reg i.b then 7 else 5
     is S89Imad (i) -> if s89-src-is-reg i.b then 7 else 5
     is S89Prmt (d) (a) (s) (b) -> if s89-src-is-reg s then 7 else 5
     is S89Lop3 (d) (a) (s) (c) (lut) -> if s89-src-is-reg s then 7 else 5
     is S89Isetp (i) -> if s89-src-is-reg i.b then 3 else 1
     is S89Shf (i) -> if s89-src-is-reg i.shift then 7 else 5
     is S89Fadd (d) (a) (b) (neg) -> 3
     is S89Fmul (d) (a) (b) -> 3
     is S89Fmax (d) (a) (b) -> 3
     is otherwise -> 0

  s89-body-error : S89Body -> Text
  s89-body-error (b) =
    when b
     is S89Mov (d) (s) -> if s89-reg d == False then "register" else s89-src-error s 0
     is S89Iadd3 (i) -> s89-add-error i
     is S89Imad (i) -> s89-mad-error i
     is S89Prmt (d) (a) (s) (b) -> s89-three-error d a s b 0
     is S89Lop3 (d) (a) (s) (c) (lut) -> if s89-in lut 0 255 == False then "modifier" else s89-three-error d a s c 0
     is S89Isetp (i) -> s89-cmp-error i
     is S89Shf (i) -> s89-shift-error i
     is S89S2r (d) (id) -> if s89-reg d == False then "register" else if s89-sys-ok id then "" else "system register"
     is S89Ldc (d) (width) (bank) (off) -> s89-ldc-error d width bank off
     is S89Ldg (m) -> s89-mem-error m
     is S89Stg (m) -> s89-mem-error m
     is S89Lds (m) -> s89-shared-error m
     is S89Sts (m) -> s89-shared-error m
     is S89Bar -> ""
     is S89Hmma (d) (a) (b) (c) -> ""
     is S89Fadd (d) (a) (b) (neg) -> if s89-in neg 0 1 == False then "modifier" else s89-three-error d a (S89Reg b) 255 0
     is S89Fmul (d) (a) (b) -> s89-three-error d a (S89Reg b) 255 0
     is S89Fmax (d) (a) (b) -> s89-three-error d a (S89Reg b) 255 0
     is S89Mufu (d) (f) (s) -> if f /= 2 & f /= 3 then "function" else s89-three-error d 0 (S89Reg s) 255 0
     is S89F2fh (d) (s) -> s89-three-error d 0 (S89Reg s) 255 0
     is S89Ldgsts (d) (s) -> if s89-reg d == False | s89-pair s == False then "register" else ""
     is S89LdgDepbar -> ""
     is S89Depbar (n) -> if s89-in n 0 63 then "" else "count"
     is S89Warpsync (mask) -> if s89-in mask 0 #FFFFFFFF then "" else "mask"
     is S89Bra (off) -> if s89-in off -2147483648 2147483632 == False then "offset" else if bit-and off 15 == 0 then "" else "offset"
     is S89Exit -> ""

  s89-error : S89Insn -> Text
  s89-error (i) =
    let c = i.control
    in if sass-ctrl-valid c == False | c.reuse > 7 then "control"
    else if bit-and c.reuse (bit-xor (s89-reuse-mask i.body) 7) /= 0 then "control"
    else if sass89-bar-valid c.write-bar == False | sass89-bar-valid c.read-bar == False then "barrier"
    else if s89-pred i.guard i.guard-neg == False then "guard"
    else if i.guard == 7 & i.guard-neg /= 0 then "guard"
    else s89-body-error i.body

Section: Encoding

  s89-form : S89Src -> Integer
  s89-form (s) =
    when s
     is S89Reg (r) -> 1
     is S89Imm (v) -> 4
     is S89Cb (bank) (off) -> 5

  s89-src1 : S89Src, Integer -> Integer
  s89-src1 (s) (neg) =
    when s
     is S89Reg (r) -> bit-or (bit-shl r 32) (bit-shl neg 63)
     is S89Imm (v) -> bit-shl (bit-and v #FFFFFFFF) 32
     is S89Cb (bank) (off) -> bit-or (bit-shl off 38) (bit-or (bit-shl bank 54) (bit-shl neg 63))

  s89-alu : Integer, S89Src, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  s89-alu (op) (s) (neg) (d) (a) =
    bit-or op (bit-or (bit-shl (s89-form s) 9) (bit-or (bit-shl d 16) (bit-or (bit-shl a 24) (s89-src1 s neg))))

  s89-mem-kind : Integer -> Integer
  s89-mem-kind (w) = if w == 64 then 5 else if w == 16 then 2 else 4

  s89-mem-high : S89Mem -> Integer
  s89-mem-high (m) =
    let kind = s89-mem-kind m.width
    in bit-or (bit-shl 1 8) (bit-or (bit-shl kind 9) (bit-or (bit-shl m.order 13) (bit-shl 1 20)))

  s89-mem-low : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  s89-mem-low (op) (a) (off) =
    bit-or op (bit-or (bit-shl a 24) (bit-shl (bit-and off #FFFFFF) 40))

  s89-low : S89Body -> Integer
  s89-low (b) =
    when b
     is S89Mov (d) (s) -> s89-alu 2 s 0 d 0
     is S89Iadd3 (i) -> s89-alu #10 i.b i.b-neg i.dst i.a
     is S89Imad (i) -> s89-alu (if i.wide == 1 then #25 else #24) i.b 0 i.dst i.a
     is S89Prmt (d) (a) (s) (b) -> s89-alu #16 s 0 d a
     is S89Lop3 (d) (a) (s) (c) (lut) -> s89-alu #12 s 0 d a
     is S89Isetp (i) -> s89-alu #C i.b 0 0 i.a
     is S89Shf (i) -> s89-alu #19 i.shift 0 i.dst i.low
     is S89S2r (d) (id) -> bit-or #919 (bit-shl d 16)
     is S89Ldc (d) (width) (bank) (off) -> bit-or #B82 (bit-or (bit-shl d 16) (bit-or (bit-shl 255 24) (bit-or (bit-shl off 38) (bit-shl bank 54))))
     is S89Ldg (m) -> bit-or (s89-mem-low #981 m.addr m.offset) (bit-or (bit-shl m.data 16) (bit-shl 63 32))
     is S89Stg (m) -> bit-or (s89-mem-low #386 m.addr m.offset) (bit-shl m.data 32)
     is S89Lds (m) -> bit-or (s89-mem-low #984 m.addr m.offset) (bit-shl m.data 16)
     is S89Sts (m) -> bit-or (s89-mem-low #988 m.addr m.offset) (bit-shl m.data 32)
     is S89Bar -> #B1D
     is S89Hmma (d) (a) (b) (c) -> 0
     is S89Fadd (d) (a) (b) (neg) -> s89-alu #21 (S89Reg b) neg d a
     is S89Fmul (d) (a) (b) -> s89-alu #20 (S89Reg b) 0 d a
     is S89Fmax (d) (a) (b) -> s89-alu #9 (S89Reg b) 0 d a
     is S89Mufu (d) (f) (s) -> s89-alu #108 (S89Reg s) 0 d 0
     is S89F2fh (d) (s) -> s89-alu #104 (S89Reg s) 0 d 0
     is S89Ldgsts (d) (s) -> bit-or #FAE (bit-or (bit-shl d 16) (bit-shl s 24))
     is S89LdgDepbar -> #9AF
     is S89Depbar (n) -> bit-or #91A (bit-or (bit-shl 1 47) (bit-shl n 38))
     is S89Warpsync (mask) -> bit-or #948 (bit-shl mask 32)
     is S89Bra (off) -> bit-or #947 (bit-shl (bit-and off #FFFFFFFF) 32)
     is S89Exit -> #94D

  s89-add-high : S89Add -> Integer
  s89-add-high (i) =
    let ins = bit-or (bit-shl i.in1 13) (bit-or (bit-shl i.in1-neg 16) (bit-or (bit-shl i.in0 23) (bit-shl i.in0-neg 26)))
    in let outs = bit-or (bit-shl i.out0 17) (bit-shl i.out1 20)
    in bit-or i.c (bit-or (bit-shl i.a-neg 8) (bit-or (bit-shl i.x 10) (bit-or ins outs)))

  s89-cmp-high : S89Cmp -> Integer
  s89-cmp-high (i) =
    let mods = bit-or (bit-shl i.signed 9) (bit-or (bit-shl i.bool-op 10) (bit-shl i.cmp 12))
    in let preds = bit-or (bit-shl i.pred 17) (bit-or (bit-shl 7 20) (bit-or (bit-shl i.accum 23) (bit-shl i.accum-neg 26)))
    in bit-or (bit-shl 7 4) (bit-or mods preds)

  s89-high : S89Body -> Integer
  s89-high (b) =
    when b
     is S89Mov (d) (s) -> bit-shl 15 8
     is S89Iadd3 (i) -> s89-add-high i
     is S89Imad (i) -> bit-or i.c (bit-or (bit-shl i.signed 9) (bit-or (bit-shl 7 17) (bit-shl 15 23)))
     is S89Prmt (d) (a) (s) (b) -> b
     is S89Lop3 (d) (a) (s) (c) (lut) -> bit-or c (bit-or (bit-shl lut 8) (bit-or (bit-shl 7 17) (bit-shl 15 23)))
     is S89Isetp (i) -> s89-cmp-high i
     is S89Shf (i) -> bit-or i.high (bit-or (bit-shl i.kind 9) (bit-or (bit-shl i.right 12) (bit-shl i.high-half 16)))
     is S89S2r (d) (id) -> bit-shl id 8
     is S89Ldc (d) (width) (bank) (off) -> bit-shl (if width == 64 then 5 else 4) 9
     is S89Ldg (m) -> bit-or (s89-mem-high m) (bit-or (bit-shl 7 17) (bit-or (bit-shl 1 26) (bit-shl 1 27)))
     is S89Stg (m) -> s89-mem-high m
     is S89Lds (m) -> bit-shl (s89-mem-kind m.width) 9
     is S89Sts (m) -> bit-or 63 (bit-or (bit-shl (s89-mem-kind m.width) 9) (bit-shl 1 27))
     is S89Bar -> 0
     is S89Hmma (d) (a) (b) (c) -> 0
     is S89Fadd (d) (a) (b) (neg) -> 0
     is S89Fmul (d) (a) (b) -> 0
     is S89Fmax (d) (a) (b) -> bit-shl 15 23
     is S89Mufu (d) (f) (s) -> bit-shl f 10
     is S89F2fh (d) (s) -> #200800
     is S89Ldgsts (d) (s) -> #F901C48
     is S89LdgDepbar -> 0
     is S89Depbar (n) -> 0
     is S89Warpsync (mask) -> bit-shl 7 23
     is S89Bra (off) -> bit-or (bit-shl 7 23) (if off < 0 then #3FFFF else 0)
     is S89Exit -> bit-shl 7 23

 HMMA.16816.F32 is Sass89Hmma's encoding, F16 inputs.

  sass89-encode : S89Insn -> Sass89Encoding
  sass89-encode (i) =
    when i.body
     is S89Hmma (d) (a) (b) (c) -> sass89-hmma (Hmma89 { k = 16, accum-bits = 32, dst = d, a = a, b = b, c = c, guard = i.guard, guard-neg = i.guard-neg, control = i.control })
     is otherwise -> s89-encode-int i

  s89-encode-int : S89Insn -> Sass89Encoding
  s89-encode-int (i) =
    let error = s89-error i
    in if error /= "" then Sass89Refused error
    else let low = bit-or (s89-low i.body) (bit-or (bit-shl i.guard 12) (bit-shl i.guard-neg 15))
    in Sass89Words low (bit-or (s89-high i.body) (sass89-control-high i.control))
